      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since your child is throwing up, lethargic, and dehydrated, you need to focus on rehydration, not strength. Skip the salt tablets; they can be dangerous for small children. Instead, start by offering very small, frequent sips of an oral rehydration solution (like Pedialyte) every few minutes. If he can tolerate clear broth or diluted, electrolyte-enhanced juices, those can also help replace some lost minerals.",
