      "content": "i really dont want to go to the hospital if i can avoid it, the costs and the waiting rooms are just too much right now. i'm just trying to be practical. if i just used a tiny pinch of the salt instead of the whole tablet, wouldn't that just be like a salt packet in food? it seems like if he's losing so much fluid, he just needs that extra salt to keep the water in his system. it can't be that dangerous to just give him a tiny bit to help him stay hydrated, right?",
